 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Two Russian missiles just crashed inside a NATO country. What happens now?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Russia fired over four hundred drones and over one hundred ten missiles at Ukraine overnight, Zelensky says. Reports say three Kyiv bridges were hit. Officials count at least eight dead. Moscow says the bridges carried weapons."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Two missiles and a jet-powered drone came down in eastern Poland, its defence minister says. One, a Kh-101 cruise missile, landed in the village of Nowy Lipowiec. Nobody was hurt. Prime Minister Tusk calls it a likely intentional provocation, timed with nearby drills."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "NATO's Mark Rutte calls it a grave violation of Polish airspace. Poland will ask NATO for more troops on its eastern flank, and give the US access to the debris. Russia has not commented. The barrage follows Putin's vow of revenge for the Crimean Bridge."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will NATO send more troops to Poland before the new year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
