 "upload": {
  "title": "Russian Missiles Crash in Poland. What Will NATO Do? #shorts",
  "description": "During a massive Russian air attack on Ukraine overnight into Friday, November 20, 2026, two Russian missiles and a jet-powered drone came down in eastern Poland, according to Polish Defence Minister Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz. Polish authorities said one Kh-101 cruise missile landed in the village of Nowy Lipowiec; a second missile came down near Rudnik nad Sanem and the drone near Mołodycz. Nobody was hurt and there was no damage to infrastructure, officials said. Prime Minister Donald Tusk said it was likely an intentional provocation, timed with the European military exercise Koalicja 2026 under way in southeastern Poland, and said the United States would get access to the debris. NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte called it a grave violation of Polish airspace. Kosiniak-Kamysz said he would ask NATO for more troops and equipment for Eastern Sentry, the mission guarding the eastern flank. Russia had not commented at the time of reporting. In Ukraine, President Zelensky said Russia launched more than 400 drones and over 110 missiles; Ukraine's Air Force gave different preliminary figures. Kyiv Mayor Vitali Klitschko said a ballistic missile damaged the Podilskyi Bridge; reports say the Darnytskyi and Southern bridges were also hit. Officials reported at least eight people killed across Ukraine (three in Kyiv, per AP) and power cuts in Kyiv and ten regions. Russia's Defence Ministry said it struck bridges used to transport weapons. The attack followed Putin's vow of a \"far more painful\" response to Ukraine's strikes on the Crimean Bridge. Casualty figures and missile counts differ between sources and may change.\n\nSources:\nAP via PBS NewsHour, Nov 20, 2026: NATO calls Russian missiles landing in Poland a 'grave violation' of airspace\nAFP via France 24, Nov 20, 2026: Poland slams Russian 'provocation' as missiles land near European military drills\nBloomberg, Nov 20, 2026: Poland Says Two Russian Missiles, Drone Crashed on Its Soil\nUPI, Nov 20, 2026: Russian missiles hit Poland amid military exercise\nSouth China Morning Post, Nov 20, 2026: Russian missiles land in Poland, as Europe holds military drills nearby\nAP via ABC News, Nov 20, 2026: Russian attacks on Kyiv kill 3, cripple bridges and cut power\nAl Jazeera, Nov 20, 2026: Russia unleashes retaliatory barrage on Kyiv bridges\nNBC News, Nov 20, 2026: Russia strikes 3 Kyiv bridges after Putin vows retaliation\nKyiv Independent, Nov 20, 2026: 2 Russian Kh-101 missiles, drone fall in Poland during Russian attack on Ukraine\n\n#geopolitics #Poland #NATO #Russia #Ukraine",
